WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
A home pregnancy test doesn't detect the embryo

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:03.840
itself.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.480
It detects a chemical that the embryo makes

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.440
and sends out.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.480
So here's the question.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.960
A sperm has just joined an egg.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.200
What has to happen next before there is

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.520
a pregnancy?

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.760
And why would a tiny embryo need to

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.040
send a message at all?

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.106
Here's where it happens in a human.

00:00:22.587 --> 00:00:25.226
An ovary releases an egg, and the egg

00:00:25.307 --> 00:00:27.946
enters the oviduct, a tube that leads to

00:00:27.987 --> 00:00:30.186
the uterus, the organ where the baby will

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:30.666
grow.

00:00:31.307 --> 00:00:34.986
Fertilisation usually happens in the oviduct, so that

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.146
is where the sperm and egg meet.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:40.866
The sperm has a tail to swim, many

00:00:40.927 --> 00:00:43.966
mitochondria that release the energy for swimming, and

00:00:44.047 --> 00:00:46.446
a cap at the front, the acrosome, that

00:00:46.527 --> 00:00:48.126
holds enzymes.

00:00:48.207 --> 00:00:50.126
The egg is large because it carries a

00:00:50.287 --> 00:00:51.486
store of food.

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:54.046
It cannot swim, so the oviduct moves it

00:00:54.247 --> 00:00:54.606
along.

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:58.473
When a sperm reaches the egg, the enzymes

00:00:58.554 --> 00:01:00.553
break down the egg's outer layer so the

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:01.993
sperm can get in.

00:01:02.314 --> 00:01:04.633
Then the nuclei of the sperm and egg

00:01:04.794 --> 00:01:05.873
come together.

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.953
One set of chromosomes plus one set makes

00:01:08.994 --> 00:01:12.153
a full two sets, in one new cell,

00:01:12.194 --> 00:01:13.113
the zygote.

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:16.253
The zygote doesn't stay still.

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:19.293
As the oviduct carries it towards the uterus,

00:01:19.374 --> 00:01:20.253
it divides.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:23.613
Each time, a cell copies its DNA and

00:01:23.694 --> 00:01:26.413
then splits, so every new cell keeps the

00:01:26.494 --> 00:01:27.893
full two sets.

00:01:28.174 --> 00:01:30.573
But the whole ball doesn't grow, because each

00:01:30.654 --> 00:01:33.373
cell splits again before it has grown, so

00:01:33.414 --> 00:01:36.093
the cells just get smaller with each split.

00:01:36.254 --> 00:01:38.733
This early splitting is called cleavage.

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:42.333
After about five days, it has become a

00:01:42.414 --> 00:01:45.133
hollow ball of cells, a blastocyst.

00:01:45.774 --> 00:01:48.493
Its outer cells will help build the placenta,

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:50.013
the organ that will link it to its

00:01:50.094 --> 00:01:52.893
mother, and a small clump inside will become

00:01:52.974 --> 00:01:55.933
the embryo, the earliest form of the baby.

00:01:57.134 --> 00:02:00.253
Next, the blastocyst needs somewhere to go.

00:02:00.574 --> 00:02:02.733
The wall of the uterus has a lining,

00:02:02.814 --> 00:02:05.373
rich in blood vessels, and that lining is

00:02:05.454 --> 00:02:08.013
its way in to the mother's supply.

00:02:08.174 --> 00:02:10.413
After the egg is released, the lining stays

00:02:10.494 --> 00:02:13.133
thick for about two weeks, but it welcomes

00:02:13.214 --> 00:02:15.293
a blastocyst for only a few of those

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:16.253
days.

00:02:16.374 --> 00:02:17.933
So what keeps it thick?

00:02:19.134 --> 00:02:20.253
A hormone does.

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:23.693
A hormone is a chemical messenger: one organ

00:02:23.814 --> 00:02:26.093
makes it, the blood carries it, and it

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:28.573
changes what another organ does.

00:02:28.654 --> 00:02:30.893
When the egg was released, the small sac

00:02:30.974 --> 00:02:33.213
that held it stayed behind in the ovary

00:02:33.254 --> 00:02:36.093
and became the corpus luteum, which means yellow

00:02:36.174 --> 00:02:37.133
body.

00:02:37.214 --> 00:02:40.653
The corpus luteum releases the hormone progesterone, and

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:43.613
progesterone keeps the lining thick and ready.

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:47.873
The blastocyst reaches the lining and attaches.

00:02:48.114 --> 00:02:50.513
Its outer cells grow into the lining, and

00:02:50.594 --> 00:02:52.313
the lining closes over it.

00:02:52.594 --> 00:02:54.273
This is implantation.

00:02:54.754 --> 00:02:57.113
A pregnancy begins from this point.

00:02:57.474 --> 00:02:59.553
From now on the embryo can begin to

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:01.953
take food and oxygen from the lining around

00:03:02.034 --> 00:03:04.233
it, as well as what the egg carried.

00:03:04.514 --> 00:03:06.673
As the placenta forms, it will get them

00:03:06.754 --> 00:03:07.793
from its mother's blood.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:11.113
Implantation is not fertilisation.

00:03:11.314 --> 00:03:13.153
It happens about a week later, in the

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:14.193
uterus.

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:16.673
And if the lining isn't ready, the blastocyst

00:03:16.754 --> 00:03:19.473
can't attach, and no pregnancy begins.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.100
But the corpus luteum is short-lived.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.900
In a month with no pregnancy, it breaks

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.900
down about two weeks after the egg is

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:28.540
released.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.740
Progesterone falls, and the lining is shed.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.260
That's a period.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.900
If that happened now, the lining would be

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.740
shed and the pregnancy would end.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.580
So the embryo sends a message.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.260
Once it is implanting, its outer cells make

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:45.660
a hormone called hCG.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:48.780
The blood carries hCG to the ovary, and

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:51.900
it tells the corpus luteum to keep working.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:55.740
So progesterone keeps flowing, and the lining stays.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:58.460
hCG acts on the corpus luteum.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:00.913
Progesterone acts on the lining.

00:04:00.967 --> 00:04:03.580
And hCG is the chemical a pregnancy test

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:04.300
detects.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.900
The corpus luteum doesn't last long enough for

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.860
a whole pregnancy, so a new organ takes

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:11.500
over.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.620
As the embryo grows, the placenta forms where

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:17.420
it attached, built from the embryo's tissue and

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.700
the mother's lining.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.860
Over the first two to three months after

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:25.020
fertilisation, the placenta takes over making the progesterone,

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.220
and the pregnancy no longer depends on the

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.380
corpus luteum.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.560
Early in pregnancy, the developing baby is called

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.520
an embryo, while its organs are forming.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.840
Later it is called a fetus, while it

00:04:37.973 --> 00:04:39.920
grows and matures.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.960
Later in pregnancy, the placenta feeds the fetus

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.320
like this.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.800
The mother's blood and the baby's blood flow

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:50.000
close together, with thin membranes between them, but

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.680
they don't mix.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:54.000
Oxygen moves from the mother's blood, where there

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.800
is more of it, into the baby's blood.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.720
Nutrients cross too.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.360
Carbon dioxide and other wastes go the other

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:01.840
way.

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:03.906
Your turn.

00:05:04.107 --> 00:05:05.506
Three situations.

00:05:05.787 --> 00:05:08.746
One: in a clinic, an egg is fertilised

00:05:08.827 --> 00:05:10.906
in a dish and grows normally into a

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:11.786
blastocyst.

00:05:12.427 --> 00:05:14.506
It is placed in a woman's uterus, but

00:05:14.587 --> 00:05:17.146
her body is making no progesterone, and none

00:05:17.227 --> 00:05:17.786
is given.

00:05:18.427 --> 00:05:20.586
What do you predict will happen, and why?

00:05:21.467 --> 00:05:24.986
Two: a woman's corpus luteum stops working three

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:26.666
weeks after fertilisation.

00:05:27.307 --> 00:05:30.266
The embryo is healthy and is making hCG,

00:05:30.347 --> 00:05:31.786
and no hormones are given.

00:05:32.427 --> 00:05:34.506
What do you expect to happen, and why?

00:05:35.307 --> 00:05:38.186
Then, what if the corpus luteum stopped working

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:40.186
five months after fertilisation?

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:44.506
Three: a student writes, "In the placenta, the

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:47.466
mother's blood flows into the fetus's blood, delivering

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:48.106
oxygen."

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:50.586
What is wrong with this, and how does

00:05:50.667 --> 00:05:52.586
oxygen really get to the fetus?

00:05:53.227 --> 00:05:55.226
Pause the video if you'd like more time.

00:07:10.634 --> 00:07:14.713
One, the blastocyst can't implant, so no pregnancy

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:15.753
begins.

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:18.473
The embryo is fine, but progesterone is what

00:07:18.554 --> 00:07:21.273
keeps the lining thick and ready, so without

00:07:21.434 --> 00:07:23.433
it the lining isn't ready to receive the

00:07:23.594 --> 00:07:24.873
blastocyst.

00:07:24.954 --> 00:07:27.673
If you said hCG would fix it, remember

00:07:27.754 --> 00:07:30.313
that the embryo makes hCG once it is

00:07:30.474 --> 00:07:34.153
implanting, and this blastocyst can't implant, so there

00:07:34.234 --> 00:07:36.553
is no hCG to rescue anything.

00:07:37.767 --> 00:07:40.886
Two, at three weeks the pregnancy is likely

00:07:40.967 --> 00:07:41.726
to end.

00:07:42.007 --> 00:07:44.006
The corpus luteum was the main source of

00:07:44.127 --> 00:07:47.686
progesterone, so progesterone falls and the lining is

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:48.726
shed.

00:07:48.807 --> 00:07:51.686
hCG can't help, because the corpus luteum it

00:07:51.767 --> 00:07:54.086
acts on has stopped working.

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:57.046
At five months, the pregnancy carries on, because

00:07:57.087 --> 00:08:00.086
the placenta now makes the progesterone.

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:03.606
If you said hCG keeps the lining, separate

00:08:03.687 --> 00:08:05.046
the two jobs.

00:08:05.167 --> 00:08:08.806
hCG keeps the corpus luteum going, and progesterone

00:08:08.887 --> 00:08:09.926
keeps the lining.

00:08:11.134 --> 00:08:14.173
Three, the two blood supplies don't mix.

00:08:14.574 --> 00:08:17.133
They flow side by side with thin membranes

00:08:17.334 --> 00:08:19.853
between them, and oxygen moves from the mother's

00:08:19.934 --> 00:08:22.413
blood, which has more of it, across into

00:08:22.494 --> 00:08:23.613
the fetus's blood.

00:08:24.834 --> 00:08:27.233
The egg is released, and the corpus luteum

00:08:27.314 --> 00:08:29.793
makes progesterone to get the lining ready.

00:08:30.034 --> 00:08:31.793
The blastocyst implants.

00:08:32.034 --> 00:08:34.993
The embryo makes hCG, which keeps the corpus

00:08:35.034 --> 00:08:36.193
luteum going.

00:08:36.434 --> 00:08:39.153
Then the placenta takes over the progesterone.

00:08:39.394 --> 00:08:43.633
To keep the hormones straight, progesterone is pro-gestation,

00:08:43.754 --> 00:08:45.713
because it holds the lining so a pregnancy

00:08:45.794 --> 00:08:46.833
can go on.

00:08:46.914 --> 00:08:49.553
And hCG is the embryo's message to the

00:08:49.634 --> 00:08:50.873
corpus luteum.

00:08:51.234 --> 00:08:54.513
Next time: how birth starts, and why labour

00:08:54.594 --> 00:08:55.393
speeds up.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.040
Here are the key notes.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:00.120
Pause the video if you need more time

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.000
to copy them.
